What if Elden Ring and God of War had a child? It's name would be Black Myth Wukong. It's not a strictly speaking souls-like game, but a souls-inspired or souls-infused game. They are doing their own thing and they are doing it great!

I'm amazed by the quality of this game; the love for the folklore; the amount of work that was put in to create so many enemies, regions, cut-scenes. THERE ARE SO MANY BOSSES AND MINI-BOSSES it's unbelievable! This should have been the Game of the Year, but they probably didn't want to award the title to yet another RPG, after Elden Ring and Baldur's Gate... ;-;

